# End-to-End Customer Propensity Engine

An enterprise-grade, modular machine learning pipeline built to predict customer conversion propensity. This project transitions standard exploratory binary classification models into a production-ready system featuring systematic preprocessing pipelines, experiment tracking, and automated model deployment logic.

## Key Features & Architecture

* **Modular Execution Pipeline:** Completely decoupled from interactive notebooks into clean, production-ready Python modules (`main.py` orchestrator and encapsulated `src/` modules).
* **Data Leakage Mitigation:** Implemented a robust preprocessing, scaling, and categorical encoding architecture using Scikit-Learn wrapper pipelines, ensuring strict separation of training/validation splits within a 5-fold Stratified Cross-Validation framework.
* **Systematic Experiment Tracking:** Integrated an **MLflow** tracking server backend to programmatically monitor hyperparameter search grids, tuning iterations, and out-of-sample evaluation metrics.
* **Automated Deployment Gatekeeper:** Engineered a programmatic "Champion-Challenger" model registry workflow. The system queries the local MLflow metadata database, evaluates incoming candidate models against the active production baseline, and dynamically handles model version promotions to `Production`.
* **State Preservation:** Captures feature pipeline configurations into a serialized state file (`models/feature_processor.joblib`) to ensure downstream inference matches model training transformations perfectly.

---

## Tech Stack & Dependencies

* **Language:** Python 3.12+
* **Environment Management:** Conda virtual environments
* **Core Libraries:** Scikit-Learn, MLflow, Joblib, Pandas, NumPy
* **Algorithms Maintained:** * Baseline: Tuned Logistic Regression (`solver='saga'`, `penalty=['l1', 'l2']`)
  * Production Champion: Histogram-Based Gradient Boosting Classifier (Peak Validation ROC-AUC: **0.8626**)

---

## Project Structure

```text
Customer Propensity Modelling/
├── data/
│   └── Bank Marketing - UC Irvine ML Repo.csv  # Raw data source
├── models/
│   └── feature_processor.joblib                # Serialized preprocessing state
├── mlruns/                                     # Local MLflow backend tracking database
├── src/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── data/
│   │   └── data_loader.py                      # Data ingestion and train/test split
│   ├── features/
│   │   └── feature_engineering.py               # Preprocessing pipelines & custom wrappers
│   └── models/
│       └── train_model.py                      # Training blocks, MLflow loops & deployment logic
├── main.py                                     # Pipeline execution orchestrator
└── requirements.txt                            # Explicit environment dependencies


## Setup and Installation

1. Clone the Repository & Navigate to Project Root
git clone [https://github.com/your-username/customer-propensity-modelling.git](https://github.com/your-username/customer-propensity-modelling.git)
cd "customer-propensity-modelling"

2. Set Up Virtual Environment & Ingest Dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

3. Execute the Full Pipeline
python main.py

4. Launch the Tracking UI
mlflow ui
Once initialized, navigate to http://127.0.0.1:5000 in your web browser.

